QueueKeeperExecutor::checkUpkeep()
├── Given the executor is paused
│   └── It should return false
├── Given the Controller, ExitQueue, or AMM is paused
│   └── It should return false
├── Given a priced batch in the scan window has unprocessed requests
│   ├── When the Controller can afford at least one request
│   │   └── It should return true with ProcessRequests and the batch ID
│   └── When the Controller cannot afford any request
│       └── It should skip the batch
├── Given the cursor batch is empty or past MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
│   ├── When a later batch in the peeked window is affordable
│   │   └── It should return true with ProcessRequests for the later batch
│   ├── When no ProcessRequests or PriceBatch work remains but the cursor can advance
│   │   └── It should return true with AdvanceCursor
│   └── When more than MAX_BATCH_SCAN skippable batches pin the stored cursor
│       └── It should advance via AdvanceCursor then process beyond the old window
├── Given the current batch has unprocessed requests
│   ├── When the batch is younger than minBatchAge
│   │   └── It should return false
│   ├── When the settlement price would violate the AMM deviation guard
│   │   └── It should return false
│   └── When the batch is old enough and the price is in band
│       └── It should return true with PriceBatch and the current batch ID
└── Given no batch needs work
    └── It should return false

QueueKeeperExecutor::performUpkeep()
├── When the caller is not the registered Forwarder
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorOnlyForwarder
├── Given the executor is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── When performData encodes PriceBatch
│   ├── When the batch ID is not the current batch
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   ├── When the current batch is younger than minBatchAge
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   └── When the current batch is old enough
│       ├── It should advance the cursor past skippable batches
│       ├── It should call Controller.priceBatch
│       └── It should emit QueueUpkeepPerformed
├── When performData encodes ProcessRequests
│   ├── When no request is affordable
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   └── When requests are affordable
│       ├── It should process the affordable prefix capped at maxUsersPerUpkeep
│       ├── It should advance the batch cursor past skippable batches
│       └── It should emit QueueUpkeepPerformed
├── When performData encodes AdvanceCursor
│   ├── When the cursor cannot advance
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   ├── When the encoded target batch ID is unreachable by the live recompute
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   └── When empty or post-commitment batches sit at the cursor
│       ├── It should advance nextBatchIdToProcess
│       └── It should emit QueueUpkeepPerformed
└── When performData encodes an unknown action
    └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorUnknownAction

QueueKeeperExecutor::setForwarder()
├── When the caller lacks ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── When the forwarder is the zero address
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorZeroAddress
└── When the caller has ADMIN_ROLE and the forwarder is valid
    ├── It should update the forwarder
    └── It should emit ForwarderChanged

QueueKeeperExecutor::setMinBatchAge()
├── When the caller lacks ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── When the value exceeds MIN_BATCH_AGE_UPPER_BOUND
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorInvalidConfig
└── When the value is valid
    ├── It should update minBatchAge
    └── It should emit MinBatchAgeChanged

QueueKeeperExecutor::setMaxUsersPerUpkeep()
├── When the caller lacks ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── When the value is zero
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorInvalidConfig
└── When the value is valid
    ├── It should update maxUsersPerUpkeep
    └── It should emit MaxUsersPerUpkeepChanged

QueueKeeperExecutor::advanceBatchCursor()
├── When the caller lacks ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── When the target is at or behind the current cursor
│   └── It should revert with QueueKeeperExecutorBatchCursorPrecedesCurrent
├── When the target is past the live (unpriced) batch
│   └── It should revert with QueueKeeperExecutorBatchCursorPastCurrent
└── When the target is valid
    ├── It should advance nextBatchIdToProcess
    └── It should emit BatchCursorAdvanced
